gpu_draw_identity_memo (off by default, hot reload; works on the draws of 0107's cached indirect buffers): each such draw
has an identity, its DRAW operation and occurrence in the frame, and a memo of what IssueDraw derived for it: pixel
shader use, shader variants and translations, pipeline and root signature, color mask, viewport, used textures and the
texture bindings (keys and textures, reused while no texture was destroyed and the scaled resolve state is unchanged).
The memo is reused when the shaders are the same and a 64-bit hash of the render state (0x2000-0x23FF but the resolve
registers) and of the used textures' fetch constants matches; float, bool and loop constants are not inputs of any of
it. Primitive processing, the render target cache update, vertex buffer residency, constant uploads and bindings stay
per draw. gpu_frame_stats logs the memo's hits and misses and the time IssueDraw takes per draw, by section and by kind
of draw (without an identity, memo hit, memo miss, identity with the memo off), and the subsections of UpdateBindings,
RequestTextures and the render target cache Update per draw, with how often each had work to do.

